What to actually implement:
-- In Vendor:new(), add:
self.vipOnly = false  -- if true, requires VIP flag to access this vendor

-- New function on Marketplace:
function Marketplace:canAccessVendor(playerName, vendorName, playerFlags)
    local vendor = self:findVendor(vendorName)
    if not vendor then return false end
    if vendor.vipOnly and not playerFlags.vip then
        return false, "VIP membership required"
    end
    return true
end
Then your VIP vendors sell cosmetics only — outfits, car liveries, emotes, name tags. Nothing in ItemDB that gives a combat edge.
The Tebex webhook hits your Node API, flips players.vip = true in the DB, and the Lua server checks that flag via exports.player:GetPlayer(source).vip before allowing access.
